.TH FUTEX 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
futex \- invokes linux futex with a timeout pointer as the fourth argument
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/futex.h>
.B int futex(int* address, int operation, unsigned int value, const struct timespec* timeout, int* address2, unsigned int value3);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Invokes Linux futex with a timeout pointer as the fourth argument. Futex words must be aligned 32-bit integers; operations and flags define the meanings of all arguments. Use futex_value when the fourth argument is an integer.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR futex (2)
